# Vendored: Authum

This directory is a pinned, vendored snapshot of the Authum SSO service.
B05-identity.sh builds a local Docker image from it -- the installer never
clones an external repo at install time (reproducible, offline-capable).

Upstream:  Authum repository (WebAuthn/passkey + Argon2id password,
           Traefik forward-auth, single-file PHP)
Commit:    e778c4d  (tag v1.0.2)
Date:      2026-07-16
Version:   1.0.2

Contents:
  src/index.php        verbatim from upstream -- the single-file application
  nginx.conf           verbatim from upstream -- fastcgi to php-fpm, denies /.git /.env
  supervisord.conf     verbatim from upstream -- runs php-fpm + nginx
  Dockerfile           NOT verbatim -- carries one deliberate local patch, see below

## The Dockerfile is patched. Do not overwrite it.

1.0.7 pins the base image to php:8.3.36-fpm-alpine (CVE-2026-109618 and
CVE-2026-109619). Keep the base on an exact patch release: the image is built
once per VERSION, so a floating tag never picks up a PHP security fix on an
installed node. A PHP security release means raising the pin and VERSION together.

## src/index.php is ahead of upstream (read before any re-vendor)

The rule below says fix upstream, then re-vendor. It has not held: 1.0.3 to 1.0.5
were made here, and the upstream repository stands at 1.0.1. 1.0.6 is made
here too: sessions in /app/data/sessions (the data volume) instead of /tmp, the
collector tied to AUTHUM_SESSION_LIFETIME instead of PHP's 24 minutes, the idle
limit checked on the server and renewed by use, and an absolute limit
AUTHUM_SESSION_MAX_AGE (30 days) that the cookie carries. A re-vendor that copies
the upstream index.php over this one undoes all of it; port upstream changes into
this file.
Test: tests/authum-session-lifetime.test.sh.
1.0.7, here too: the session cookie is Secure unless AUTHUM_AUTH_URL is http
(a local node on plain http), and the passkey options name the auth URL as the
origin, the value the server already checks against.
1.0.8, here too: on a local node (an http auth URL) the sign-in page names the
launcher "Open Smart Node", the way in for an owner with no password or passkey.
1.0.9, here too: on a local node the sign-in page shows no username and password
form, only that line (interface map and look audit, 2026-10-30).
1.0.11: the sign-in page links the shared UI kit from the Workspace (/welcome/ui/)
instead of its own copy of the tokens; kit buttons and fields; dark follows the system; no
"[Settings]" corner link beside the card's own Settings button.
1.0.12: the passkey settings page on the kit too ("Sign-in settings", no "[Authum]").

`RUN docker-php-ext-install opcache` is commented out here (2026-05-27). It runs
phpize + ./configure + make inside the image and costs ~5 of B05's 8:32 wall time,
which is also ~5 minutes on every golden bake. Authum is a low-traffic admin auth
panel, so the perf gain does not pay for the build cost at this stage. Re-enable
it through a pre-built image only if profiling justifies the build cost.

This file used to claim all four files were "verbatim from upstream" AND tell you to
copy the Dockerfile straight from the upstream checkout. Following the procedure as written
silently reinstated opcache and added ~5 min per bake. Caught on 2026-07-16 during the
1.0.1 -> 1.0.2 re-vendor, only because the diff was read before committing.

## Refresh procedure

Authum is security-sensitive; the snapshot lags upstream fixes. To refresh:
  1. Copy `src/index.php`, `nginx.conf`, and `supervisord.conf` from an upstream
     checkout into this directory.
     For the Dockerfile: diff it against upstream and port real upstream changes by
     hand, KEEPING the opcache line commented. Never copy it wholesale.
  2. Update the Commit / Date above to the new upstream HEAD.
  3. Bump STAGE_VERSION and the AUTHUM_IMAGE default tag in B05-identity.sh
     so installed nodes rebuild on the next --verify/run.

Do not edit the vendored files in place -- fix upstream, then re-vendor.
